<title>USA: Gilead names Donald Rumsfeld chairman.</title>
<headline>Gilead names Donald Rumsfeld chairman.</headline>
<dateline>FOSTER CITY, Calif. 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gilead Sciences Inc said Friday that board member Donald Rumsfeld will succeed retiring chairman Michael Riordan, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Rumsfeld joined Gilead as a director in 1988. Before that, he was chief executive of Monsanto Co's pharmaceutical unit, G.D. Searle &amp; Co. He is a board member of ABB AB, Gulfstream Aerospace Corp, Kellogg Co, Sears, Roebuck and Co and Tribune Co, Gilead said.</p>
<p>Riordan, who founded Gilead in 1987, will continue to serve as a board director, the company said.  </p>
<p>Rumsfeld was the 13th U.S. Secretary of Defense, the company   said. He also has served four terms in the U.S.</p>
<p>Congress and is a  former U.S. Ambassador to the NATO and a former White House Chief ofStaff.</p>
<p>Rumsfeld received the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 1977.</p>
</text>
